==============================================================================
FACE SPLIT: clock Z/n half-turn (2-torsion) vs shell Z/(2n-1) antipodal-freeness
==============================================================================
 n | n even? | clock half-turn n/2 (sigma-fixed 2-torsion) | shell 2n-1 | (2n-1) odd => no fixed pt | block q=4n-5 [odd]
  5 | False   | none (n odd: only 0 fixed)               |   9      | True (always)            | 15
  6 | True    | r=3  (= n/2, the half-turn leak)         |  11      | True (always)            | 19
  7 | False   | none (n odd: only 0 fixed)               |  13      | True (always)            | 23
  8 | True    | r=4  (= n/2, the half-turn leak)         |  15      | True (always)            | 27
  9 | False   | none (n odd: only 0 fixed)               |  17      | True (always)            | 31
 10 | True    | r=5  (= n/2, the half-turn leak)         |  19      | True (always)            | 35
 11 | False   | none (n odd: only 0 fixed)               |  21      | True (always)            | 39
 12 | True    | r=6  (= n/2, the half-turn leak)         |  23      | True (always)            | 43
 13 | False   | none (n odd: only 0 fixed)               |  25      | True (always)            | 47
 14 | True    | r=7  (= n/2, the half-turn leak)         |  27      | True (always)            | 51
 15 | False   | none (n odd: only 0 fixed)               |  29      | True (always)            | 55

=> shell 2n-1 and block q=4n-5 are ALWAYS ODD: antipodally free (genuine 2-orbits, no self-partner).
   The clock n carries the half-turn self-partner n/2 exactly when n is EVEN (n=14: r=7).
